There are toasts but no result overlay! It's been 1.4s; expected result at 0.9s. State says mode finished. Maybe overlay is shown but hidden behind? The screenshot shows toasts and finish gate; no modal. Could be because `showResult` isn't called? In frame, mode finished branch increments finishTimer and calls showResult after 0.9; but we also have a separate increment inside render (`finishTimer += 1/60`, mode finished) that could call. Actually render has a block:
```
if (mode === 'finished') {
 finishTimer += 1/60;
 if (!finishedShown && finishTimer > 0.85) showResult();
}
```
This was leftover duplicate. showResult sets overlay open. Why not visible?

Maybe the result overlay is open but behind the `#screens`? #screens no active screens; z-index 30, overlay z-index 40 so above. Toast z 50 appears above. Modal should be centered.

Wait, maybe showResult sets modal but the overlay `is-open` class is added; CSS `.overlay` display grid; should show. But it isn't. Check DOM classes via eval and computed style. Maybe `showResult` early returns because `mode !== 'finished'`? mode finished. Or `finishedShown` true? Initially false. Hmm.

Also toasts are at top-right; the achievement toasts stack; expected.

Let's inspect with eval: `document.querySelector('#overlay-result').className`, computed opacity, innerText, result values.

