content.text:
Note media ordering: appended editor media queries right after max-width 430 block, before max-height 620 landscape existing block. Both apply. Our max-width 620 blocks before tall landscape max-height. Fine. But the later existing max-height 620 landscape has `.btn` etc. no conflict.

Now the JS. Let's construct carefully.

Add editor state and functions after writeSave, before canvas? But editor functions need `view`, canvas, TILE, etc. We can declare state after save; functions later. `loadEditor` uses THEMES. Fine. We'll insert:

```
const EDITOR_DEFAULT = { ... };
...
let editor = loadEditor();
...
```

Need import TILE. Currently imports createPlayer, stepPlayer, SIZE, FLOOR_Y, CEIL_Y, DEATH_TIME. Add TILE.

Also customPlaytest state.

Let's design the exact code block.

```
const EDITOR_KEY ...
const EDITOR_MIN_LENGTH = 1400;
const EDITOR_MAX_LENGTH = 40000;
const EDITOR_DEFAULT_NAME = 'Custom Run';

const EDITOR_TOOL_TIPS = {...};

function defaultEditor() {
 return { v:1, name: 'Custom Run', theme:'dawn', speed:400, length:6000, objects:[], shards:[] };
}
```
Default speed maybe 360 to match level 1. Speed selector values 300,360,400,440,480. Use 360.

Sanitize:
```
function sanitizeEditor(raw) {
 const base = defaultEditor();
 if (!raw || typeof raw !== 'object') return base;
 base.name = typeof raw.name==='string' ? raw.name.trim().slice(0,24) || base.name : base.name;
 base.theme = THEMES[raw.theme] ? raw.theme : base.theme;
 base.speed = clamp(Number(raw.speed)||base.speed, 240, 520);
 base.length = clamp(Number(raw.length)||base.length, 1400, 40000);
 const used = new Set();
 let n = 0;
 const nextId = (t) => { let id; do { id = `custom-${t}-${++n}`; } while(used.has(id)); used.add(id); return id; };
 if (Array.isArray(raw.objects)) {
  for (const o of raw.objects.slice(0, 800)) {
    if (!o || typeof o !== 'object') continue;
    const x = clamp(Number(o.x)||0, -2000, 40000);
    if (o.type === 'spike') {
      const size = clamp(Number(o.size)||TILE, 24, 88);
      const dir = o.dir === -1 ? -1 : 1;
      const y = clamp(Number(o.y)|| (dir===1?FLOOR_Y:CEIL_Y), -200, FLOOR_Y+200);
      base.objects.push({ id: nextId('spike'), type:'spike', x, y, size, dir });
    } else if ... block ...
  }
 }
 if (Array.isArray(raw.shards))...
 return base;
}
```
Need validate types and values. Use Number.isFinite to avoid NaN. helper `num(v, fallback)`. Could be concise.

Blocks: w,h clamp 22..TILE*12 maybe; y clamp -200..FLOOR_Y.

Saw: r clamp 16..64; y clamp.
Pad: w clamp 30..120.
Orb: r 22, kind yellow.
Portal: kind gravity/speed, w 54, h etc; mul for speed clamp 0.8..1.8, gravity.
Action types preserve IDs? We assign new IDs; fine.

Shards:
```
for raw.shards slice 0..100:
 x clamp, y clamp; { id: nextId('shard'), x, y, taken:false }
```
No object+shard ID collision matters only objects use Set separately. The engine uses only object IDs for used sets; shard IDs are used to track runShardIds and save. Duplicate shard ids could matter only display; assign unique.

Load:
```
function loadEditor() {
 let raw=null;
 try { raw=JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(EDITOR_KEY)); } catch {}
 return sanitizeEditor(raw);
}
```
Persist:
```
let editorSaveTimer=0;
let editorDirty=false;
function persistEditor({silent=true}={}) {
 clearTimeout(editorSaveTimer); editorSaveTimer=0;
 try { localStorage.setItem(EDITOR_KEY, JSON.stringify({v:1,name:editor.name,theme:editor.theme,speed:editor.speed,length:editor.length,objects:editor.objects,shards:editor.shards.map(({taken,...s})=>s)}));} catch {}
 editorDirty=false; updateEditorUI();
 if (!silent) { toast('cube','LEVEL SAVED',`${editor.name} — ${editor.objects.length} objects`,'✦'); }
}
```
Wait toast kind values: toast classes `toast-cube` etc. Use 'cube' for cyan-ish purple. Or 'award'. Use cube.

`updateEditorUI()` defined later but function declaration hoisted.

Editor state:
```
const editor = {
 ...loadEditor(),
 camX: 0,
 tool: 'spike',
 hover: null,
 dragging: false,
 lastCell: '',
 panStartX: 0,
 panStartCam: 0,
 undo: [],
 clearArmed: 0,
};
```
But editor object includes v. Fine.

However `editor` is const but properties mutate.

Need `editorFinishX`:
```
function editorFinishX() {
 let maxX = 0;
 for (const o of editor.objects) maxX = Math.max(maxX, o.x + (o.w || o.size || (o.r*2) || 0));
 for (const s of editor.shards) maxX = Math.max(maxX, s.x);
 return clamp(Math.max(editor.length, maxX + 900), 1400, 40000);
}
```
Careful: `o.w || o.size || o.r*2` for spikes size 44 so maxX = x+44. For portals w. Good.
But if user set finish at 2000 and objects to 2500, finish 3400. Fine.

`editorMaxCam`:
```
const max = Math.max(0, editorFinishX() + 700 - view.logicalW * 0.8);
```
If view logical width 1500, at finish 6000, max = 6700-1200=5500, so finish can be at x=5500+? visible width ends 7000. Fine. For start no panning left.

`clampEditorCam`:
```
editor.camX = clamp(editor.camX, 0, editorMaxCam());
```

`setEditorTool(tool)`:
- validate keys in TOOL_TIPS
- toggle buttons .is-active and aria-pressed
- editor.hover = null? Keep.
- update tip.
- audio.sfx('click').

`updateEditorUI()`:
- count text `${objects.length} OBJECT${s} · ${shards.length} ♦`; maybe show finish distance. Use `${objects.length} OBJ · ${shards.length} ♦`.
- status: dirty 'UNSAVED' else 'SAVED', class toggle.
- select values if not input focused? Sync theme/speed/name:
```
if ($('#editor-theme').value !== editor.theme) ...
if (document.activeElement !== $('#editor-name')) $('#editor-name').value = editor.name;
...
```
Careful initial boot; elements exist.
- `#editor-speed` options values, set.
- tool active classes.
- tip text.
- `#editor-count` maybe show `12 OBJ · 3 ♦ · 61m`. Let's include finish: `${...} · ${Math.round(editorFinishX()/100)}M`. Good.

`buildEditorOptions()`:
```
const themeSel=$('#editor-theme'); themeSel.innerHTML = Object.keys(THEMES).map(...).join('');
const speedSel=$('#editor-speed'); [300,360,400,440,480]...
```
Theme labels names: Map keys to labels:
`{dawn:'STEREO DAWN', rush:'NEON RUSH', circuit:'CIRCUIT', gravity:'GRAVITY', overdrive:'OVERDRIVE', time:'TIME MACHINES', ystep:'YSTEP', clutter:'CLUTTERFUNK'}`. Could also add a "custom" theme? All 8.
Speed values. Use `[300,360,400,440,480]`.

Event listeners for selects will be added in wiring:
```
$('#editor-theme').addEventListener('change', (e)=>{editor.theme=e.target.value; queueEditorSave();});
$('#editor-speed').addEventListener('change', ... parseFloat)
$('#editor-name').addEventListener('input', ...)
```
Add in boot or after functions. Need `buildEditorOptions` called before adding listeners? Either.

`queueEditorSave()`:
```
editorDirty = true; updateEditorUI();
clearTimeout(editorSaveTimer);
editorSaveTimer = window.setTimeout(()=>persistEditor({silent:true}), 300);
