Potential issue: `drawEditorMarker` used `roundRect` which begins path then fill then stroke; after fill, path still intact. Fine.

Now input. Modify keydown at top, canvas pointerdown branch, add pointermove/wheel/pointerleave, pointerup. Click actions. Editor options listeners. Boot.

Keydown current:
```
window.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {
  const jumpKey = ...
  if (jumpKey) {...}
  if (e.code === 'Escape') {...}
});
```
Insert editor block at start:
```
if (mode === 'editor') {
 const tag = document.activeElement?.tagName;
 if ((e.code==='KeyS') && (e.ctrlKey||e.metaKey))...
 if (e.code==='Escape'){ exitEditor(); return; } // but if input focused, Esc maybe blur? Still exit.
 if (tag==='INPUT'||tag==='SELECT') return; // allow typing/arrow in selects
 if (e.code==='KeyZ' ...)...
 if (e.code==='Delete'||e.code==='Backspace')...
 if arrows/A/D...
 return;
}
```
If Ctrl+Z while input focused, should allow text undo maybe. So check input first for most keys, but Ctrl+S maybe still save. For Escape while input focused, blur? Could exit editor; maybe fine. Let's implement:
```
if (mode === 'editor') {
 const editingField = document.activeElement && ['INPUT','SELECT','TEXTAREA'].includes(...);
 if ((e.ctrlKey||e.metaKey) && e.code==='KeyS') { e.preventDefault(); persistEditor({silent:false}); return; }
 if (e.code === 'Escape') { e.preventDefault(); if(editingField) document.activeElement.blur(); else exitEditor(); return; }
 if (editingField) return;
 if ((e.ctrlKey||e.metaKey) && e.code==='KeyZ') { prevent; undoEditor(); return; }
 if (e.code==='Delete'||e.code==='Backspace') { prevent; if(editor.hover){pushEditorUndo(); eraseEditorAt(editor.hover);} return; }
 if (arrow left/right/A/D) { prevent; editor.camX = clamp(editor.camX + dir*editorPanStep()*(e.shiftKey?2:0.5),...) ; return;}
 if (e.code==='KeyR') ??? no.
 return;
}
```
For backspace maybe browser navigation; prevent.

Pan keyboard A/D conflicts with typing only if input focused (handled). Good.

Canvas pointerdown:
```
if (mode==='editor'){ editorPointerDown(e); return;}
if (mode!=='playing') return;
```
Canvas pointermove:
```
canvas.addEventListener('pointermove', (e)=>{ if(mode==='editor') editorPointerMove(e); });
```
Wheel.
pointerleave.

Global pointerup add.

Click handler add tool/pan actions and editor actions. Order:
- sound
- level/cube
- tool button
- pan
- action
Data-action for editor save etc.

Add:
```
const toolBtn = e.target.closest('[data-tool]');
if (toolBtn) { setEditorTool(toolBtn.dataset.tool); return; }
const panBtn=...; if(panBtn){audio.sfx('click'); editor.camX=clamp(editor.camX+Number(panBtn.dataset.pan)*editorPanStep(),0,editorMaxCam()); return;}
```
Then actions:
```
else if (action === 'editor') { audio.sfx('click'); enterEditor(); }
else if (action==='editor-exit'){ enter? exitEditor(); }
else if (action==='editor-save'){ persistEditor({silent:false}); }
else if (action==='editor-test'){ startCustomPlaytest(); }
else if (action==='editor-undo'){ undoEditor(); }
else if (action==='editor-clear'){ clearEditor(); }
```
Note `audio.ensure()` is called before actions. `persistEditor({silent:false})` also calls audio.sfx click. fine.

Retry action custom:
```
if (action==='retry') {
 hideOverlay(...);
 if (customPlaytest) startCustomPlaytest(); else startLevel(current.id);
}
```
Next action uses startLevel normal, custom hidden.

