Add near UI wiring after `$('#btn-pause')...`:
```
$('#editor-theme').addEventListener('change', ...)
$('#editor-speed')...
$('#editor-name').addEventListener('input', ...)
```
`queueEditorSave` updates UI; name field guard.

`pagehide` add flush editor:
Current `window.addEventListener('pagehide', writeSave);` change to function that also persists. Could edit to:
```
window.addEventListener('pagehide', () => { writeSave(); if (mode === 'editor' || customPlaytest) persistEditor({silent:true}); });
```
But `persistEditor` clears timer. Fine. Also visibilitychange if hidden while editor, persist. Add there.

Boot: call `buildEditorOptions(); updateEditorUI();` after refresh. But updateEditorUI calls editorFinishX and `$('#editor-status')` exists. Good. Add before updateSoundButtons maybe. Also `updateEditorUI` sets tool active and tip. Fine.

Potential issue `buildEditorOptions` sets theme select innerHTML then updateEditorUI sets value. good.

